# The studio's secrets, as NAME=value lines. Install as a root-only file (the studio reads it as root, then runs as
# the node user, who can't open it again):
#   sudo install -m 400 -o root -g root secrets.env.example secrets.env && sudoedit secrets.env
# Back this file up with the data: without STUDIO_SECRET_KEY a restored studio can't read its saved keys.

# 64 random hex characters: openssl rand -hex 32. Keep it for the life of the studio.
STUDIO_SECRET_KEY=

# Only for admin-password sign-in (no SSO proxy): 16+ characters, known only to admins.
# STUDIO_PASSWORD=

# Optional: a second proof that a request came through your proxy, for setups where its address can change
# (Kubernetes). The proxy sends it in the X-Studio-Proxy-Secret header.
# STUDIO_PROXY_SECRET=
